  "review_decisions": [
    "Use nonnegative coefficients for positive span; distinguish an open positive-scaling cone from a cone containing its vertex.",
    "Separate positive nonlinear amplitude realization from unrestricted signed linearized increments and retain their quadratic remainder.",
    "Keep centered probabilistic covariance distinct from uncentered velocity products, and specify which variables are averaged before phase evaluation.",
    "State exponential-tilt derivative identities inside the open finite-moment domain, with strict variance positivity only for a nonconstant observable.",
    "Give quantitative hypotheses for square roots at flat boundaries instead of assuming every smooth nonnegative function has a smooth square root.",
    "Moment targets with slow parameters are functions, not finitely many sampled values.",
    "Supported radial inverses require the corresponding weighted integral to vanish; their support can fill gaps between source bumps.",
    "Prove power-moment independence using ordered positive supports and make inverse deterioration at coalescing exponents explicit.",
    "Reuse scalar and vector log-MGF owners and repair their elementary exponential/logarithmic prerequisites.",
    "Give a quadratic small-solution estimate and separate zeroth-order existence from higher parameter regularity.",
    "Variance monotonicity of a normalized exponential weight does not alone imply unbounded variance; state the distinction explicitly.",
    "Defer the auxiliary-shifted radial primitive and its arbitrary-order cancellation to B13; the ordinary supported radial inverse and compatibility projection are included here.",
    "The one linear-algebra subject-index basis-label scope finding predates this batch and concerns related existing theorem owners; leave that unrelated label unchanged."
  ],
